    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall with increased fall risk (Z91.81)</content>. A mechanical fall at a hazard, on a background of reduced leg strength and balance (Timed Up and Go 13.5 seconds, chair stand 9, tandem stance 6 seconds at intake). No orthostatic hypotension, no medicines, and normal vitamin D and B12. Geriatric medicine agrees and found no other cause. [S]<list><item>Home physical therapy for strength and balance twice a week for 12 weeks, with a qualified tactile interpreter at sessions, starting next week.</item><item>Occupational therapy home safety visit, requested today.</item><item>Until then, avoid the back steps and walk outdoors with her guide.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lifelong deafblindness (H54.0X55)</content>. Her communication access plan is now recorded in the chart. [S]<list><item>Hospital communication passport written with her in braille and print.</item><item>Interpreter booked by the clinic for every visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall history</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No further falls</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Timed Up and Go, 30-second chair stand, and four-stage balance test</td><td>At assessment, then after the exercise program</td><td>Up to date</td><td>At intake: Timed Up and Go 13.5 seconds, chair stand 9, tandem stance 6 seconds; repeat at the three-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Orthostatic blood pressure</td><td>At assessment, then if symptoms</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication review for fall-risk drugs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No medicines, prescribed or over the counter</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Feet and footwear</td><td>At assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal; well-fitting lace-up shoes</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Vitamin D</td><td>At assessment</td><td>Up to date</td><td>31 ng/mL at intake; no supplement needed for fall prevention</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Vision check</td><td>At assessment</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Lifelong blindness; mobility is supported by touch, rails, and a sighted guide instead</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Bone density (DXA) for women 65 and older</td><td>Once, then by risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Femoral neck T-score -1.9 and spine -1.4: low bone mass. FRAX 15 percent major and 2.4 percent hip, below treatment thresholds</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Strength and balance exercise program</td><td>12 weeks, then ongoing</td><td>Referred</td><td>Home physical therapy twice a week with an interpreter</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Home hazard assessment</td><td>After a fall</td><td>Referred</td><td>Occupational therapy home visit requested</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Comprehensive geriatric assessment</td><td>Once, after a fall at this age</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen by geriatric medicine today</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Qualified tactile interpreter booked by the clinic, double-length visit, braille materials</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Interpreter present for the whole visit; after-visit summary given in braille</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>No further falls, and a 30-second chair stand of 12 or more by the six-month review. In progress; target 2026-09-14 [S]</item><item>Home changes complete: handrails on both sides of every step, tactile edge strips, and vibrating smoke and carbon monoxide alarms with a bed shaker. In progress; target 2026-09-14 [S]</item><item>A communication access plan in her chart: a qualified tactile interpreter booked by the clinic for every visit, double-length appointments, braille after-visit summaries, and a hospital communication passport. Outcome by 2026-03-23: Plan recorded and passport written in braille and print [S]</item><item>Keep traveling to speak, with a travel plan for falls and illness. In progress; target 2026-09-14 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: STEADI (Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths and Injuries): Clinical Resources (2024); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024); Zhou SY, et al. Training Medical Students in Deaf, DeafBlind, and Hard-of-Hearing Patient Care Through Interactive Lecture and Simulation. MedEdPORTAL 2025;21:11566 (2025); Osteoporosis to Prevent Fractures: Screening (2025)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Physical therapy starts next week; occupational therapy home visit to be scheduled. Falls review in about three months. Call after any fall. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-15: three-month falls prevention and function review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
